commit_sha":"1d194995f0835a8fb9ded93eb22e1dcde7d2e62a","position":"1785424025704697537-413ff86e-283b-4ec6-8811-dbcd40e2c418"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":"claude-code_2-1-220_agent","claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":"d1ad70ed-ce91-4b63-9f32-e6b36aea17d4","comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Fix implemented and pushed for review: https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/1044 (change 1044, commit f822315). Root cause: the 228b DET-floor short-circuit (c781127a2) blocks a DET-failing plan with zero finder calls, so test_plan_review_reuse's fixture (a plan with no AC checklist, DET-blocked by design) stopped exercising the LLM tier — test_force_bypasses_verdict_reuse and test_code_change_reruns_full_review failed on 'calls > first_calls' (0 > 0). Fix (tests only): the fixture plan now passes the DET floor (proper '## Acceptance Criteria' checklist) and the counting fake manufactures the BLOCK from the LLM tier — an F1 finding (blocking posture, threshold 0.60) verified full-yes at high severity, so Pass-3 decides 'block'. All 7 tests in the file keep their original semantics; audited the whole file for the same latent assumption (the two render tests use literal dicts, unaffected). Gates: file + tests/unit/workflow/test_det_short_circuit.py green, make lint + make typecheck clean. Awaiting LLM-Review/Verified.","timestamp":1785423333467872001}],"created_at":1785422750073713001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"a8e38593-b224-417f-b693-2b4b316f1557","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"7e77-cbe5-5bcf-4096"},{"link_uuid":"7fde7e4c-d0e8-4974-838c-5797cda390c5","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"6917-3024-4b86-44ce"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\nChanges 1031 (228b: DET-floor short-circuit, c781127a2) and 1035 (7e77: BLOCK-verdict reuse, 517e0470a) are individually green but semantically interact: tests/unit/test_plan_review_reuse.py::test_force_bypasses_verdict_reuse and ::test_code_change_reruns_full_review assert the full review invokes the finder (calls > 0), but their fixture plans do not pass the deterministic floor (P1 AC checklist), so the now-landed short-circuit returns a BLOCK with zero finder calls. Main is red for every subsequent change whose tree contains both commits (observed: Verified -1 on 1041, 1039, 1040). CI run: 30540561663.\n\n## Approach\nFix the test fixtures, not the code: give the two tests' fixture plans a DET-floor-passing shape (a `## Acceptance Criteria` checklist with valid items) so a bypassed/invalidated reuse genuinely reaches the LLM passes, preserving each test's intent (--force reruns the full review; a code change reruns the full review). Audit the rest of test_plan_review_reuse.py for the same latent assumption. No production code changes.\n\n## Scope\ntests/unit/test_plan_review_reuse.py\n\n## Testing\nThe two failing tests pass with the finder invoked; the full tests/unit/test_plan_review_reuse.py suite passes; a spot-run of tests/unit/workflow/test_det_short_circuit.py confirms no regression.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] test_force_bypasses_verdict_reuse and test_code_change_reruns_full_review pass on a tree containing both c781127a2 and 517e0470a (checked: `pytest tests/unit/test_plan_review_reuse.py`).\n- [ ] All other tests in the file pass unmodified in intent (checked: same pytest run).","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[{"path":"tests/unit/test_plan_review_reuse.py","reason":"fix fixture plans to pass DET floor"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","managed_refs":[["parent","a492-3e46-ca44-40a5"],["relates_to","6917-3024-4b86-44ce"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"a492-3e46-ca44-40a5","parent_status_uuid":"129c6460-04a5-4953-ba0f-4b6155d59938","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"2c38-bef7-b045-4ecc","ticket_type":"bug","title":"reuse tests break under DET short-circuit (post-1031/1035 main)","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["3617e3b4-5e22-4233-aadc-e7c9f21d9c3c","a8e38593-b224-417f-b693-2b4b316f1557","cb21c4c5-da32-4d6d-8f81-0b7ad6c66a2a","129c6460-04a5-4953-ba0f-4b6155d59938","9f879893-da6b-40b2-a635-9066174e7ef4","7009de05-979e-415c-a4ae-b4d44a9a2140","413ff86e-283b-4ec6-8811-dbcd40e2c418","7fde7e4c-d0e8-4974-838c-5797cda390c5"]},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1785424562820857783,"uuid":"7cdd4cf0-9432-4870-966f-71cd1386b61f"}